# devflow (packages/devflow): GitHub, for the package's own steps *inside* this container — the
# device-flow login (github.com), the REST and Git Data APIs (api.github.com), and the tarball a
# checkout is fetched as (api.github.com redirects to codeload.github.com; lib/remote.py streams it).
#
# Asked once whether these are leftovers, since `scripts/packages.sh` clones on the HOST and needs
# nothing here. Two different consumers, and only the first is host-side: fetching the *package* is
# a git clone by the operator; talking to GitHub about a *task* is evaluate / integrate / publish,
# which are `type: script` steps and run wherever Conductor runs — the main agent, on this list.
# Measured: from the main agent api.github.com 200, codeload 301, github.com 200; from a profile
# container both refused, because a profile carries its own list and none of them names GitHub.
# devflow's own RUNBOOK lists this entry as required instance setup (OPERATIONS §59).
^github\.com$
^api\.github\.com$
^codeload\.github\.com$
